(7759639, 1284681, 12611, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Yo_Spiff:</b></div><hr/><i> Looks like someplace in the New England area. I recall similar canals and buildings when I visited Lowell, Ma for work. I always like the contrast of a cool disk sky with warm light. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is an office building in Watertown CT- (where my office is located)- it was called the Princeton Knitting Mills in the early 20th/late 19th century, and when the dye colors were changed, the river also ran that color... <br/> <br/>Tis the season for strong blue skies and complimentary warm yellows and oranges.</td>', 'Originally posted by Yo_Spiff: Looks like someplace in the New England area. I recall similar canals and buildings when I visited Lowell, Ma for work. I always like the contrast of a cool disk sky with warm light.   It is an office building in Watertown CT- (where my office is located)- it was called the Princeton Knitting Mills in the early 20th/late 19th century, and when the dye colors were changed, the river also ran that color...  Tis the season for strong blue skies and complimentary warm yellows and oranges.', '2023-11-04 11:48:53.000000', NULL, 0),
